## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests ability to design a privacy-aware, multi-stage pipeline with governance and cross-account considerations.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven architecture; S3 event filtering; Transcribe with diarization; Comprehend PII redaction; SageMaker multi-task inference; DynamoDB composite keys; KMS encryption; Glue lineage; DLQ design; cross-account IAM trust policies.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Orchestrator triggered on S3 PUT event
async function handle(event) {
  const { bucket, key } = event.Records[0].s3;
  const callId = extractCallId(key);
  const transcribeJob = await startTranscribe(bucket, key, callId);
  await pollUntilComplete(transcribeJob.JobId, onTranscribeComplete);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy guarantees end-to-end and simulate PII leakage scenarios?
- How would you detect and mitigate model drift across languages in production?
- What retry and timeout strategies would you implement for each service call?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design a scalable, multi-tenant AI moderation pipeline on AWS with policy-driven routing, data isolation, and compliant audit logging.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model endpoints and per-tenant routing
- DynamoDB for policy storage; S3 for audit logs and artifacts
- Tenant isolation via prefixes, IAM scoping, KMS encryption
- Step Functions for orchestration, error handling, retries
- Cost controls: autoscaling, model cache, off-peak scheduling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-routing logic for tenant-aware inference
function routeToEndpoint(tenantId, itemType) {
  const policy = fetchPolicy(tenantId)
  if (itemType === 'image') return { endpoint: policy.imageEndpoint, threshold: policy.imageThreshold }
  return { endpoint: policy.textEndpoint, threshold: policy.textThreshold }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test tenant policy overrides without affecting others?
- How would you enforce data deletion and retention across S3 and DynamoDB?
